;; FQ-FREEVAR-GUARD-1 / CALL-PRE-ARGCALL-1. The witness that carries TWO free
;; symbols, in two different positions, so one cell pins both halves of the check.
;;
;; `dispatch` has the let-bound projection of letproj.llmll, so its three body
;; constraints name `s` through an environment binder. It also passes a CALL
;; RESULT to a tag-preconditioned callee, and the call-pre constraint it emits
;; carries the branch path condition while its env omits the binder that
;; condition names, so that constraint names `_bv_p_1` in its own lhs.
;;
;; Before the guard, liquid-fixpoint answered `Constraint with free vars` four
;; times: `[s]` on constraints 1, 2 and 3 and `[_bv_p_1]` on constraint 4.
;; Cells c39 and c40 of docs/design/resp-fact-proposal.md, in one program.
;;
;; MEASURED, and recorded because it refutes the remedy the roadmap proposed for
;; CALL-PRE-ARGCALL-1: adding the omitted bind id to the call-pre's env does NOT
;; repair constraint 4. That bind's own refinement names `s`, so the constraint
;; then reports `[s]` instead of `[_bv_p_1]`. The crash moves; it does not go.
(export dispatch)
(type Ctl (| Boot) (| Ran) (| Halt))
(def-shell ctl-of [s: (int, Ctl)] -> Ctl
  (second s))
(def-shell tag-code [p: Ctl] -> int
  (pre (= p Ran))
  (post (>= result 0))
  1)
(def-shell dispatch [s: (int, Ctl)] -> int
  (post (>= result 0))
  (let [(p (second s))]
    (match p ((Boot) 0) ((Ran) (tag-code (ctl-of s))) ((Halt) 2))))
